00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.270 align:start position:0%
 
hello  everyone i hope you all are doing great  and enjoying your learning process  and either working on the project or  finished your research project  this video is to guide you towards your  project submission on the learn portal  to begin with ensure that your profile  is complete  that is you have an updated profile  picture and also linked in your social  accounts  i would be taking an example of one of  our research fellows  singh who has completed her profile with  a profile picture  linked in her linkedin account so that  we can feature her progress on  our socials and tag her and also as you  can see that in the profile  section itself we can see what all  courses has she covered  and her project submission as well so we  can see here that she has completed  a few of the courses and she can view  her certificate  in the certificate tab under her profile  section  only and download her certificate for  sure  to submit your project on the learn  portal you need to have  a score of 10 000 and only then you  would  be eligible to upload your project  on the learn portal in the profile  section itself you have a section called  projects here you have to submit the  project now let me quickly take you  through how you have to submit the  project  so what you have to do is you have to  create a presentation first of all  and record your presentation and after  recording your presentation  share the mp4 file with me i'll upload  it on a youtube channel  and share the embed code with you to  upload it  on your project section in the profile  tab  so here we begin with the steps overview  data sets abstract and so on i'll take  on one step one time  so in the overview section you have to  first of all get the title of your  project  and upload or say put in the embed code  which i would be sharing with you  and then comes the data sets part where  you have to upload  the data sets which you used for your  analysis  and the data sets have to be uploaded on  data warts  i would be again sharing a video with  you on how you can upload your data set  on database  and share the link here and then you  have to give  an abstract for your project and then  write the introduction  introduction would have an overview of  what you worked on  and also the images have to be uh  attached here with the introduction part  in the methods part you need to mention  the methodology that was used to carry  out the analysis  in your research project as you can see  akansha has also  uh used the images of a pipeline which  she  run to carry out her analysis and then  finally comes a results tab where you  have to  tell what results you obtained  also use the images upload the images  your scatter plots or whatever plots you  worked on and  uh got for your project  and then finally comes the discussion  tab  in the discussion tab you have to  mention what you  uh finally got from your result and  conclude your project  and don't forget to mention the  references because that's really  very important and finally comes the  acknowledgement time where you have to  give  acknowledgement to your mentor and  whatever support you got  throughout your project so that is the  easiest way of uploading your project  on the learn portal and once you upload  your project on the learn portal  you would be uh your project would be  visible  to all of the people on the learn portal  as you  as you can see that we already have a  lot of submissions of projects by now  and the submissions are there on the  portal and you can  also go through each and every project  and get an idea  of how our research fellows worked on  different sorts of analysis  and got the results for your reference  i'll share the link  of the projects part on the portal  in the comments section in the  description  of the video looking forward to your  project submission

